 "T_tot_def": "T_tot = dT_cmblens + dT_tsz + dT_cib + dT_ksz per band (T_tot_parts)",
 "coords": "simulation HEALPix (theta, phi) of the HalfDome lightcone, the same frame for the display images and the value maps; NOT Galactic (l, b)",
 "projection": {
  "applies_to": "the display JPEGs only (the value maps are HEALPix: value_maps)",
  "type": "equirectangular (plate carree), full sky",
  "coords": "simulation HEALPix (theta, phi) of the HalfDome lightcone; NOT Galactic (l, b)",
  "rows": "row 0 is theta = 0 (the simulation north pole); theta increases downwards",
  "columns": "phi increases to the right from 0 at the left edge (the mirror image of the usual astronomical longitude-increases-left convention)",
  "pixel_centres": "theta_i = (i + 0.5) pi / H, phi_j = (j + 0.5) 2 pi / W"
 },
 "display": {
  "width": 4096,
  "height": 2048,
  "lo_width": 1024,
  "lo_height": 512,
  "note": "JPEG colour images for viewing only (not for values). _dk = dark-centred diverging variant for overlays. tSZ display shows |dT|."
 },
 "value_maps": {
  "layout": "healpix",
  "nside": 512,
  "ordering": "RING",
  "npix": 3145728,
  "width": 2048,
  "height": 1536,
  "pixel_index": "the PNG holds the RING-ordered pixel array row-major: sample k (row k // 2048, column k % 2048) is HEALPix RING pixel k (width = 4 NSIDE, height = 3 NSIDE)",
  "lookup": "value at (theta, phi) = the sample of pixel ang2pix_ring(nside, theta, phi) (healpy.ang2pix(nside, theta, phi); SkyCore.ang2pixRing in the browser), theta = colatitude from the simulation north pole, phi = longitude, both in the display images' frame; no interpolation",
  "pixel_area_arcmin2": 47.21026754312813,
  "pixel_size_arcmin": 6.870972823634811,
  "format": "PNG, 16-bit grayscale, non-interlaced (samples big-endian as in every PNG; rows use the standard adaptive filters 0-4)",
  "decode": "v [muK] = vmin + (vmax - vmin) * u / 65535",
  "encode": "u = round((clip(v, vmin, vmax) - vmin) / (vmax - vmin) * 65535)",
  "clip": "vmin, vmax = the 0.05 and 99.95 percentiles of the map's pixels (equal areas, so these are sky-area percentiles); clip_frac = sky-area fraction outside [vmin, vmax]",
  "pixel_value": "mean over the pixel area of the field band-limited to l <= 3000 (cosine taper 2500-3000), computed as the plain mean of the 16 NSIDE-2048 sub-pixels of each NSIDE-512 pixel (equal areas; = healpy.ud_grade); no smoothing",
  "resolution": {
   "pixel": "HEALPix NSIDE 512 (RING), equal areas",
   "pixel_area_arcmin2": 47.21026754312813,
   "pixel_size_arcmin": 6.870972823634811,
   "smoothing": "none",
   "effective_fwhm_arcmin": 5.080922740408475,
   "effective_fwhm_axes_arcmin": {
    "equator": [
     4.745294634399623,
     5.449873539974543
    ],
    "mid_latitude_50deg": [
     4.366627649175865,
     5.96545098783559
    ],
    "polar_cap_20deg": [
     4.001626967658484,
     6.604376963314531
    ],
    "pole": [
     4.427541211465899,
     5.821110706494824
    ]
   },
   "effective_def": "Gaussian-equivalent (second-moment) FWHM of the 2 arcmin instrument beam and the pixel average: effective_fwhm_arcmin takes the pixel as a square of the same area, sqrt(beam^2 + (8 ln 2 / 12) area); effective_fwhm_axes_arcmin gives [minor, major] from the second moments of actual pixels (pixel_fwhm_axes). The l <= 3000 taper is not included.",
   "taper": {
    "ell_lo": 2500,
    "ell_hi": 3000,
    "why": "kept at l = 2500-3000 for the NSIDE-512 value maps. (1) It is the field the display images show, so eye and ear get the same field (the ear its 6.87-arcmin pixel means) and one NSIDE-2048 synthesis serves both. (2) The pixel mean suppresses higher l strongly: extending to the beam-limited l <= 6000 would add 4.8 per cent to the stored variance of a CIB-143-like map (each pixel changing by 0.20 sigma rms), 0.6 per cent for tSZ- and kSZ-like maps (0.07 sigma), and would need NSIDE-4096 syntheses to keep the area-mean quadrature accurate. (3) A lower taper would remove power the pixel means should contain: 1250-1500 (~2.5 NSIDE, no power above the pixel scale) would remove 36 per cent of the stored CIB variance, 13 (tSZ) and 15 (kSZ) per cent. Power between ~1.5 NSIDE and l = 3000 stays in each pixel mean as pixel-scale structure; nothing is interpolated between pixel centres, so this \"aliasing\" creates no artefact. (Synthetic Gaussian realizations of the cls_cache.npz spectra, stretched to 1/4 scale, 64 sub-pixels per pixel; 2026-11-13.)"
   },
   "replaces": "v2: 2048x1024 equirectangular cells (10.5 arcmin, narrowing as sin(theta)) of the field smoothed by a 13.2-arcmin Gaussian, effective 15.1 arcmin"
  },
  "units": "muK, thermodynamic temperature, beam-convolved (2 arcmin FWHM); monopole kept",
  "stats": "mean_uK, median_uK, sigma_uK (std about the mean) and rms_uK (about zero) are taken over the pixels of the STORED map (equal areas): use sigma_uK for loudness weights. tSZ and CIB have a large monopole (the median is the empty-sky level), so |v - median_uK|/sigma_uK is quiet where the sky is empty. sigma_field_uK: see sigma_field.",
  "sigma_field": "sigma_field_uK = sqrt(sum_{l>=1} (2l+1) C_l / 4 pi), C_l = healpy alm2cl of the alm that was synthesized (band-limited and tapered; for T_tot the summed alm): the std about the mean of that continuous field before pixel averaging and quantization, so sigma_uK is below it by the pixel window (most for the high-l CIB and tSZ)",
  "shared_files": "tSZ entries share two files (+y and -y orientation) and differ only in vmin/vmax; decode them like any other entry."
 },
